# Unraid API actions the `unraid` MCP server exposes to Claude: read-only only.
# One canonical runraid action per line; becomes UNRAID_RMCP_ENABLED_TOOLS.
# runraid rejects unknown names at start, so a typo fails loudly.
#
# Left out on purpose even though they only read: api_keys, api_key, the
# api_key_*/permission helpers, oidc_*, is_sso_enabled, validate_oidc_session
# (auth configuration and secrets); vars, config, settings, flash,
# registration, rclone (configuration that can hold credentials or license
# data); connect, remote_access, cloud, me, owner, servers (account data);
# display, customization, public_theme, time_zone_options, is_fresh_install,
# internal_boot_context, assignable_disks, plugin_install_operation(s) (no
# admin value). All write actions are left out.
#
# Not a boundary on its own: the API key's permissions are. See README,
# "Unraid API".
